      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: block workspace dotenv endpoint overrides [AI]",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users starting OpenClaw in a workspace with a `.env` file could have endpoint-style connector routing values loaded from that workspace differently than other host-routing controls.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nWorkspace dotenv filtering already blocks connector host and base URL override suffixes. This change extends the same shared suffix rule to `_ENDPOINT` keys so endpoint routing stays in trusted shell, global dotenv, or explicit config paths rather than workspace dotenv files.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can keep using trusted environment variables and config for connector endpoints, while workspace `.env` files no longer supply `_ENDPOINT` routing values. Non-control workspace variables continue to load normally.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/dotenv.test.ts` passed locally through the Codex-worktree focused fallback: 33 tests passed.\n- Remote Crabbox/Testbox validation was unavailable on this host because no `crabbox` or `blacksmith` binary was installed.\n\nAI-assisted change.\n",
